**Advanced: Semantic Chunking**

```javascript
// For better results, chunk by semantic boundaries
function semanticChunk(text, maxTokens = 8000) {
  // Split by double newlines (paragraphs)
  const paragraphs = text.split(/\n\n+/);

  const chunks = [];
  let currentChunk = [];
  let currentSize = 0;

  for (const para of paragraphs) {
    const paraSize = estimateTokens(para);

    // If single paragraph is too big, split by sentences
    if (paraSize > maxTokens) {
      if (currentChunk.length > 0) {
        chunks.push(currentChunk.join('\n\n'));
        currentChunk = [];
        currentSize = 0;
      }

      const sentences = para.split(/(?<=[.!?])\s+/);
      let subChunk = [];
      let subSize = 0;

      for (const sentence of sentences) {
        const sentSize = estimateTokens(sentence);
        if (subSize + sentSize > maxTokens && subChunk.length > 0) {
          chunks.push(subChunk.join(' '));
          subChunk = [];
          subSize = 0;
        }
        subChunk.push(sentence);
        subSize += sentSize;
      }

      if (subChunk.length > 0) {
        chunks.push(subChunk.join(' '));
      }
    } else if (currentSize + paraSize > maxTokens) {
      chunks.push(currentChunk.join('\n\n'));
      currentChunk = [para];
      currentSize = paraSize;
    } else {
      currentChunk.push(para);
      currentSize += paraSize;
    }
  }

  if (currentChunk.length > 0) {
    chunks.push(currentChunk.join('\n\n'));
  }

  return chunks;
}
```

**Key Takeaways:**
1. **Estimate tokens conservatively** - 4 chars/token is a safe approximation
2. **Reserve space for response** - always leave room for the output
3. **Overlap chunks for continuity** - prevents losing context at boundaries
4. **Prefer semantic boundaries** - paragraphs are better than arbitrary cuts
5. **Monitor conversation length** - trim old messages when approaching limits

